    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF144 CSSStyleProperties docs]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41254</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41254"/>
        <updated>2025-09-23T22:48:18.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF144 (and Safari) implement <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code>. This is a derived class of <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> that represents the inline or computed styles on an element. It exists because  <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> is now going to be a base class from which specific types of style and rule information will be applied, and only include the relevant information for that context.</p>
<p dir="auto">Anyway, this adds the class. Note however that I have not yet updated the things that use it. I didn't think anything did, but in retrospect, Safari likely does.</p>]]></content>
