<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">There are still <a href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/39393#issuecomment-2851420219" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/39393/hovercard">several Learn articles</a> not linked from the learnsidebar. The ones we want to keep should really be linked in some way. This PR adds an "Additional tutorials" subsection at the end of the extension modules to contain the additional tutorials.</p>
<p dir="auto">In one case (performance), I didn't add it into "Additional tutorials"; I just moved the article so that the slug made more sense, and then added it into the main flow of that module.</p>
<p dir="auto">In one case (forms), I edited an article to make it a) more useful and b) actually make sense in the context of earlier forms articles in the same module (we don't want to cover all those CSS techniques only to then say "don't style form elements" in a later article).</p>

